Brine Management and Energy Efficiency Retrofit is a delivery project under target O1.T3 (Reduce non-revenue water in distribution networks below 15 percent by 2030). Retrofit plants to cut energy use per cubic metre and manage brine discharge. The project started on 2025-01-01 and is led by Saudi Water Authority.
2. Purpose of this deliverable
This requirements and design specification covers functional requirements and the target operating model. It is deliverable D2 against milestone M2, due 2025-07-15.
3. Key findings
1. Overall completion of the workstream stands at 83 percent as of the reporting date, ahead of the delivery plan.
2. Adoption by the target entities reached 72 percent, measured across the pilot group defined in the inception phase.
3. The main delivery risk is dependency on the data readiness required by O1.T3; a mitigation owner has been assigned and the item is tracked in the project risk log.
4. Recommendations
Sustain the current cadence of fortnightly delivery reviews, close the open acceptance items before milestone M3, and record the lessons learned in EnviroAI so the next phase reuses them.
