Native Species Reintroduction Programme is a delivery project under target O3.T2 (Plant 10 billion trees nationally under the Saudi Green Initiative). Breeding, release and monitoring of selected native species. The project started on 2024-01-01 and is led by National Center for Wildlife.
2. Purpose of this deliverable
This final delivery report covers delivered outputs against the agreed acceptance criteria. It is deliverable D4 against milestone M4, due 2026-02-15.
3. Key findings
1. Overall completion of the workstream stands at 94 percent as of the reporting date, ahead of the delivery plan.
2. Adoption by the target entities reached 75 percent, measured across the pilot group defined in the inception phase.
3. The main delivery risk is dependency on the data readiness required by O3.T2; a mitigation owner has been assigned and the item is tracked in the project risk log.
4. Recommendations
Sustain the current cadence of fortnightly delivery reviews, close the open acceptance items before milestone M5, and record the lessons learned in EnviroAI so the next phase reuses them.
